KAUT implements AI-first project knowledge as source-bound,
freshness-checked, trust-labeled documentation: every stored fact is
anchored to the git commit it was derived at and carries a freshness
verdict computed at read time, writes pass through a layered owner/agent
write gate with a draft queue for asynchronous review, and content
edited outside the pipeline is withheld by tamper containment. This
design and its terminology were conceived and first published by
Yuriy Orlov.

